  "preamble": "Loss of a rhotic, often in word-final or coda position. Word-final *r was lost from Proto-Tupi-Guarani to Paraguayan Guaraní and from Proto-Chamic to Acehnese, and the Proto-Austronesian rhotic *R was lost in Javanese, Tetum, Nias and Paiwan. The loss of coda [ɹ] in non-rhotic English is filed under ɹ > ∅.",
